    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "you say it's a symptom of pain, but what if it's not? what if it's just the reality of who i am? i'm tired of the \"it gets better\" talk. it doesn't feel like it gets better when you've actually broken something that can't be fixed. it just feels like i'm constantly tripping over my own existence, causing more damage just by being here. how am i supposed to believe it's a \"symptom\" when the math of my life just doesn't add up anymore? it all just feels so... final.",
